I can do it, but I don't feel comfortable making you guys do

302
00:11:55,560 --> 00:11:58,520
it, something to North Korea and Nevada.

303
00:11:58,520 --> 00:12:05,040
But it starts off voluntary and ends with.

304
00:12:05,040 --> 00:12:05,540
All right.

305
00:12:10,540 --> 00:12:12,400
We'll all say that.

306
00:12:12,400 --> 00:12:15,680
All right, but full of enthusiasm for economics,

307
00:12:15,680 --> 00:12:17,960
let us now think more about coordination.

308
00:12:17,960 --> 00:12:21,640
So remember we did that very simple coordination game,

309
00:12:21,640 --> 00:12:26,440
very simple coordination game where players can either

310
00:12:26,440 --> 00:12:27,320
go left or right.

311
00:12:27,320 --> 00:12:28,840
And if they both do the same thing,

312
00:12:28,840 --> 00:12:31,640
then it's better than if they both do different things.

313
00:12:31,640 --> 00:12:34,400
I do something left, right, left, right.

314
00:12:34,400 --> 00:12:38,360
And then if they do different things, then the payoffs are 0.

315
00:12:38,360 --> 00:12:41,080
And if they do the same thing, then it's better than 0,

316
00:12:41,080 --> 00:12:43,080
although one of the two is better, in this case,

317
00:12:43,080 --> 00:12:45,680
right, left, or 0.

318
00:12:45,680 --> 00:12:48,680
So we've got these two pure strategy Nash equilibria.

319
00:12:48,680 --> 00:12:51,880
There's also a mixed strategy Nash equilibrium here.

320
00:12:51,880 --> 00:12:53,680
I'm not going to bother proving it to you,

321
00:12:53,680 --> 00:12:55,280
but it's pretty easy to show there's

322
00:12:55,280 --> 00:12:57,520
a mixed strategy Nash equilibrium.

323
00:12:57,520 --> 00:12:59,680
But there's an interesting fact, which

324
00:12:59,680 --> 00:13:02,320
is that the mixed strategy Nash equilibrium is unstable.

325
00:13:02,320 --> 00:13:04,400
I could go through a lot of math to convince you,

326
00:13:04,400 --> 00:13:07,400
but I'm going to just, but it's very easy to do intuitively.

327
00:13:07,400 --> 00:13:12,200
So imagine that you're in a country where 51% of the people

328
00:13:12,200 --> 00:13:16,040
speak one language and 49% speak the other.

329
00:13:16,040 --> 00:13:19,080
So which language do you probably want to learn?

330
00:13:19,080 --> 00:13:19,920
51%.

331
00:13:19,920 --> 00:13:21,080
You don't speak either one.

332
00:13:21,080 --> 00:13:22,320
You want to learn the 51%.

333
00:13:22,320 --> 00:13:25,880
And as a result, the percentage that speak the language

334
00:13:25,880 --> 00:13:28,400
quickly goes to 52, and 53, and 54.

335
00:13:28,400 --> 00:13:31,520
So you very naturally go to one extreme

336
00:13:31,520 --> 00:13:33,640
where that's the one language that everybody speaks.

337
00:13:33,640 --> 00:13:34,480
On the other hand, of course, if it

338
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:38,720
started at 49% of that language, you generally go the other way.

339
00:13:38,720 --> 00:13:40,920
So the reason why the mixed strategy Nash equilibrium

340
00:13:40,920 --> 00:13:43,480
is unstable, that would be very much like a country where

341
00:13:43,480 --> 00:13:47,360
you have exactly 50% speaking one language, exactly 50%

342
00:13:47,360 --> 00:13:48,560
speaking the other language.

343
00:13:48,560 --> 00:13:51,360
If it's perfectly divided, then you're

344
00:13:51,360 --> 00:13:53,320
indifferent between both languages.

345
00:13:53,320 --> 00:13:56,200
What's unstable is that there's a little disruption.

346
00:13:56,200 --> 00:13:58,720
This is just a slight random tip.

347
00:13:58,720 --> 00:14:01,200
Then the system tends to go to all one language or all

348
00:14:01,200 --> 00:14:03,640
the other language.

349
00:14:03,640 --> 00:14:05,880
Right now, this is very different from a bargaining

350
00:14:05,880 --> 00:14:06,520
game.

351
00:14:06,520 --> 00:14:08,280
In a bargaining game, remember, I

352
00:14:08,280 --> 00:14:11,400
think we already saw that if everyone but you bargains hard,

353
00:14:11,400 --> 00:14:13,360
how do you want to bargain?

354
00:14:13,360 --> 00:14:16,000
Soft, because in a world where everyone bargains hard,

355
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:16,880
no deals are struck.

356
00:14:16,880 --> 00:14:19,880
Imagine that everyone else demands 60% of the surplus.

357
00:14:19,880 --> 00:14:21,880
Do you want to demand 60% too?

358
00:14:21,880 --> 00:14:24,640
No, then there will be no deals.

359
00:14:24,640 --> 00:14:29,880
Instead, you want to go around asking everyone for 40%.

360
00:14:29,880 --> 00:14:33,160
Now, in a world like this, if you start off

361
00:14:33,160 --> 00:14:35,920
with half the people bargaining hard, half bargaining soft,

362
00:14:35,920 --> 00:14:38,240
and split it the other way, then that's an equilibrium.

363
00:14:38,240 --> 00:14:40,120
That's a mixed strategy Nash equilibrium.

364
00:14:40,120 --> 00:14:42,400
Then if there's a little bit of random variation,

365
00:14:42,400 --> 00:14:44,760
since you go to 51% bargaining hard,

366
00:14:44,760 --> 00:14:47,480
which strategy looks better when you slightly

367
00:14:47,480 --> 00:14:50,760
increase the percentage of people bargaining hard?

368
00:14:50,760 --> 00:14:53,240
Soft, yes, which offsets.

369
00:14:53,240 --> 00:14:55,800
And that's why it is actually a stable mixed strategy Nash

370
00:14:55,800 --> 00:14:58,360
equilibrium, where if you move a little bit away,

371
00:14:58,360 --> 00:15:00,480
people want to start doing the opposite of the thing

372
00:15:00,480 --> 00:15:02,840
that became more common until you get back.

373
00:15:02,840 --> 00:15:04,960
But with the coordination game, on the other hand,

374
00:15:04,960 --> 00:15:06,520
if you move a little bit away, people

375
00:15:06,520 --> 00:15:08,480
want to just amplify that and amplify it

376
00:15:08,480 --> 00:15:11,360
until finally you go back to one of the pure strategy

377
00:15:11,360 --> 00:15:13,320
Nash equilibrium.

378
00:15:13,320 --> 00:15:14,720
Again, imagine you're in a country

379
00:15:14,720 --> 00:15:16,040
where exactly half the people drive

380
00:15:16,040 --> 00:15:18,480
on the right side of the road and half drive on the left.

381
00:15:18,480 --> 00:15:19,920
What are the more you can do?

382
00:15:19,920 --> 00:15:20,760
You're stuck in the country.

383
00:15:20,760 --> 00:15:23,080
Like, I would just not go to country in the first place.

384
00:15:23,080 --> 00:15:25,920
You show up there, ah!

385
00:15:25,920 --> 00:15:28,400
All right, if it was exactly 50-50, then you're just like,

386
00:15:28,400 --> 00:15:31,040
well, both strategies are equally deadly.

387
00:15:31,040 --> 00:15:33,440
But on the other hand, if you notice a slight imbalance,

388
00:15:33,440 --> 00:15:35,560
51% are driving on the right.

389
00:15:35,560 --> 00:15:37,880
It's like, well, it's only a slight advantage,

390
00:15:37,880 --> 00:15:40,880
but if it reduces the subsidy, though,

391
00:15:40,880 --> 00:15:44,000
there's a slight reduction in the risk that I die today,

392
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:45,320
that seems worth it.

393
00:15:45,320 --> 00:15:49,760
And so once everyone who looks at 51 sees it,

394
00:15:49,760 --> 00:15:52,760
then you might go 53, 55, 60, 80,

395
00:15:52,760 --> 00:15:55,400
and then the country saved itself purely

396
00:15:55,400 --> 00:15:58,360
through decentralized means, as people just

397
00:15:58,360 --> 00:16:00,960
want to do whatever it is that other people are doing

398
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:01,960
so that they don't die.

399
00:16:05,200 --> 00:16:08,080
So anyway, that is why the mixed strategy Nash equilibrium

400
00:16:08,080 --> 00:16:09,400
is unstable here.

401
00:16:09,400 --> 00:16:10,000
There's math.

402
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:12,440
You can do the math, but the math

403
00:16:12,440 --> 00:16:16,320
is less actually informative than just understanding

404
00:16:16,320 --> 00:16:17,800
what it's like to be in a game where

405
00:16:17,800 --> 00:16:19,680
the fact that something's becoming more common

406
00:16:19,680 --> 00:16:21,440
means that you want to do it even more,

407
00:16:21,440 --> 00:16:22,920
versus when something's becoming more common

408
00:16:22,920 --> 00:16:24,320
means that you want to do it less.

409
00:16:24,320 --> 00:16:26,120
Ones where something's becoming more common

410
00:16:26,120 --> 00:16:27,360
means you want to do it less, or ones

411
00:16:27,360 --> 00:16:29,760
that those are stable mixed strategy Nash equilibrium,

412
00:16:29,760 --> 00:16:31,760
and ones where other people want to do it more

413
00:16:31,760 --> 00:16:34,960
means you want to do it more, those are unstable.

414
00:16:34,960 --> 00:16:37,040
Questions about that?

